{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And I will make you swear by HaShem.</b> It would have been proper for Abraham to command his son Isaac not to take a wife from the daughters of Canaan, but his desire was to send to his land and his family during his lifetime, and he made the servant swear to do so during his lifetime or after his death. Therefore it was in any case necessary to make the servant swear to go there, and it was necessary to say: I command you that you shall not take a wife for my son from the daughters of Canaan, and that you shall go to my land and take a wife for him from my father's house. And since he made the servant swear to this, there was no need to command Isaac anything, for he knew of him that he would not transgress the will of his father and the oath that he made his servant take, for the matter was truly known to Isaac. It is also possible that the servant was the steward over his property, and he commanded him that he should give Isaac a wife according to his will and bequeath to him his property on that condition. And this is the reason for \"who rules over all that he has\":" "<b>The God of the heavens and the God of the earth.</b> The Holy One, blessed be He, is called the God of the land of Israel, as it is written (II Kings 17:26), \"They do not know the law of the God of the land,\" and it is written (II Chronicles 32:19), \"And they spoke of the God of Jerusalem as of the gods of the peoples of the land.\" And there is in this a sod; I will yet write it with the help of HaShem (see Leviticus 18:25). But in verse (7), \"He took me from my father's house,\" the God of the earth is not mentioned, for he was in Haran or in Ur of the Chaldees. And so the Sages said (Ketubot 110b): one who dwells outside the land is like one who has no God, as it is said (I Samuel 26:19), \"For they have driven me out today from joining the inheritance of HaShem, saying, Go, serve other gods.\""], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :register {:flags {1 ["God"]}}, :notes {0 "The text appears to be a running commentary rather than a tightly structured argument; translated as presented without reordering."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:21:34.502635116Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}